  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Seven card stud deal: two cards face down, four face up, one face down. Five betting rounds, one after each round of face-up cards and one after the final card. At showdown, to win the pot a player must have both the best five-card poker hand and the highest spade among all players; the highest spade may be any of the seven cards, not necessarily face down. If the best hand and the highest spade are held by different players, or if no one has a spade, no one wins and the pot carries over to the next deal. Only players who were in the showdown participate in the carryover deal.',
    Player: 'Seven card stud deal: two cards face down, four face up, one face down. Five betting rounds, one after each round of face-up cards and one after the final card. At showdown, to win the pot a player must have both the best five-card poker hand and the highest spade among all players; the highest spade may be any of the seven cards, not necessarily face down. If the best hand and the highest spade are held by different players, or if no one has a spade, no one wins and the pot carries over to the next deal. Only players who were in the showdown participate in the carryover deal.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by holding BOTH the best 5-card poker hand AND the highest spade among all players at showdown.',
    gameplay: 'Seven card stud deal: two cards face down, four face up, one face down. Five betting rounds, one after each round of face-up cards and one after the final card. At showdown, to win the pot a player must have both the best five-card poker hand and the highest spade among all players; the highest spade may be any of the seven cards, not necessarily face down. If the best hand and the highest spade are held by different players, or if no one has a spade, no one wins and the pot carries over to the next deal. Only players who were in the showdown participate in the carryover deal.',
    keyRules: [
      'Must hold BOTH best hand AND highest spade to win.',
      'If conditions are split between players, pot carries over.',
      'Carried-over pot grows across multiple deals â€” can become enormous.',
      'Only showdown participants play the next deal when pot carries over.',
      'Highest spade uses ANY of the 7 cards, not just hole cards.',
